# Scratch output from verification runs — screenshots, review pages, one-off
# scripts. These are produced to be LOOKED AT and then discarded; a 7 MB set of
# JPEGs was committed once by a `git add -A` and had to be removed in the next
# commit, which is exactly what these patterns prevent.
.brand-shots/
.preview-shots/
*.preview-review.html
.fpvarabic-review.html
.look.mts
.shots.mts
.final.mts
.verify.mts
.review-site/

# Netlify build output and the local deploy reproduction (scripts/testNetlifyDeploy.ts).
# Both are generated; the 35 MB function bundle in particular must never be committed.

# The gate self-check writes a throwaway publish directory here.

# Generated by the Supabase reconciliation flow: a live-schema snapshot and the
# corrective plan derived from it. Both describe ONE moment of a real project's
# state — regenerated on demand, never a source of truth.
supabase/plan/
supabase/live-snapshot.json
supabase/remote-status.json
